# Variants

Uncommitted work stays on the globe until Save. The UI word is
**variant**, never version. **Save**, never Update. How the studio
works: [docs/studio.md](docs/studio.md). Language: `CONTEXT.md`.

## The rule

Every **Save** writes a **new snapshot**. Its id is UTC unix time
(`v` + milliseconds).

- **The name is the variant.** The name field shows the active card.
  Save with that name and this snapshot is the next head. Change the
  name and Save starts another variant, keeping the ranges you were on.
  The list does not nest names.
- **Shuffle of the layout seed, or an explore tile** is a **different
  planet**. Give it a new name if it should not join the active card.
- **Shape** with no new name continues the active name.

The Variants panel shows one card per name. Earlier saves of that name
are history on the card. A catalog write never drops an id. Delete
marks the snapshot (`deleted`); the list hides it. Undo clears the
mark. Loading merges disk with the browser cache by id. The checkout
on the globe is always a card — if it is missing from the file, put it
back.

Do not reuse a snapshot id. Do not group cards by seed, parent, or
recipe. Explore likes may write **ranges** to the active snapshot as
they go; that is not a save of the planet.

## Language

**Save** — write the working planet as a new snapshot.
_Avoid_: Update, commit

**Same planet** — same layout seed. Shape iteration stays here.
_Avoid_: Generation, in-place update

**Different planet** — new layout seed, or an explore tile.
_Avoid_: Copy, save as (unless naming)

**Variant** — the named card. Snapshots of that name are its history.
_Avoid_: Fork (as a tree operation)
